cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use UBEM-MCP, please cite it as below, together with EnergyPlus-MCP (see NOTICE.md)."
title: "UBEM-MCP: Urban building energy modeling data and simulation for AI assistants"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Liang
    email: liangzhang1@arizona.edu
    affiliation: "Department of Civil and Architectural Engineering and Mechanics, University of Arizona"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/TensorBuildLab/UBEM-MCP"
url: "https://github.com/TensorBuildLab/UBEM-MCP"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, Python library and
  command line that gives AI assistants, scripts and people one tested
  interface to urban building energy modeling: building data with recorded
  provenance, archetype or user-supplied EnergyPlus models, background batch
  runs, district results, retrofit scenarios, comparison with measured energy
  use and national reference data.
keywords:
  - urban building energy modeling
  - UBEM
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - AI agents
  - EnergyPlus
  - building stock
